<title>USA: Franchise Finance files $500 mln shelf.</title>
<headline>Franchise Finance files $500 mln shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Franchise Finance Corp of America filed Friday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission a shelf offering of up to $500 million debt securities, preferred shares and common stock.</p>
<p>The Scottsdale, Ariz.-company that provides financing for restaurant chains said proceeds from the sale will be used for general corporate purposes which may include repaying outstanding debt.</p>
<p>No underwriters were named in the SEC filing.</p>
</text>
